{
  "message": "Thanks — I can proceed. For identity verification I need you to confirm 2 of the following: date of birth, email, phone number, or address. You already provided your email, so please confirm your date of birth (MM/DD/YYYY) and the phone number on file (include area code). Once you confirm those I will log the verification and then: (1) check your Light Blue checking for any pending activity or early-closure fees, (2) identify checking options that maximize the linked-savings APY while keeping strong everyday perks, and (3) if you choose, open the new checking and a savings account and (optionally) transfer the $10,000 as the opening deposit with your authorization. Please provide your DOB and phone number to continue.",
  "next_step": "User provides date of birth and phone number for verification."
}

{
  "message": "Thanks — I’ve completed the requested actions and answered your credit-card question. Summary of what I did and what I found:",
  "actions_taken": [
    "Opened a Gold Account (savings): account_id ea5af121ea163b18, status OPEN, balance $0.00, opened 11/14/2025.",
    "Opened a Blue Account (checking): account_id 44de82a09654121b, status OPEN, balance $0.00, opened 11/14/2025.",
    "Closed your Light Blue checking (chk_rp65a7b3c4) after confirming no cards or transactions: status CLOSED as of 11/14/2025.",
    "Updated your email on file to riley.parker+confirmed@gmail.com (confirmation stored)."
  ],
  "overdraft_protection": {
    "status": "NOT YET ENABLED",
    "note": "I can enable overdraft protection (automatic transfers from your Gold savings to your Blue checking) now, but you must confirm acceptance of the per-transfer fee of $12.50. Please confirm if you want me to enable it now."
  },
  "debit_card": {
    "status": "SCHEDULED",
    "note": "Blue checking debit cards can be ordered only after the checking account has been OPEN for at least 3 business days. Per your earlier preference, I will schedule a STANDARD delivery order at that time unless you tell me otherwise."
  },
  "funding": {
    "gold_savings": "Left OPEN and UNFUNDED as requested. You have 30 days to fund via external transfer before the account is closed automatically."
  },
  "credit_card_recommendation": {
    "summary": "You asked whether the Gold Rewards Card includes travel insurance and, if not, which card both includes travel insurance and gives the best relationship bonus for Gold savings.",
    "findings": [
      "Gold Rewards Card: provides a small relationship APY bonus on the Gold savings (+0.025%) and reduces the Gold Account minimum to $5,000, but documentation does NOT show that the Gold Rewards Card includes comprehensive travel insurance benefits (trip cancellation/interruption/lost baggage) as a listed benefit.",
      "Business Platinum Rewards Card and Business Platinum/Platinum Rewards Card tiers do include generous travel insurance (example: Business Platinum Rewards shows per-trip travel insurance up to $62,500). Diamond Elite and Platinum tiers also list strong travel protections in their benefit guides.",
      "Credit-card APY bonus potential: For Gold Account, the Diamond Elite Card gives +0.3% (larger than Gold Rewards Card's +0.025%). For other savings tiers, Platinum/Gold-tier cards offer varied bonuses (see Gold/Platinum docs)."
    ],
    "recommendation": "If travel insurance (trip cancellation/interruption/lost luggage) is a deal-breaker, I recommend applying for the Platinum Rewards Card or Business Platinum Rewards Card (they explicitly include robust travel insurance benefits). Between travel coverage and Gold-savings APY boost:\n- Platinum Rewards Card gives a meaningful savings APY bonus (on some accounts) and includes travel insurance; Diamond Elite gives larger APY bonuses but travel insurance details are strongest in the Platinum-tier documentation I found.\n- If you want the single-card pairing that balances travel insurance + helps your Gold savings APY, get the Platinum Rewards Card (or Business Platinum if you prefer that product); it provides travel insurance and also gives a positive APY bonus on certain savings classes."
  },
  "next_steps": "1) Confirm whether you want me to enable overdraft protection now (I will link your Gold savings to Blue checking and accept $12.50 per-transfer fee on your authorization). 2) Confirm if you want me to apply for a Platinum Rewards Card (I will proceed with the application steps) — if yes, confirm whether you prefer the personal Platinum Rewards Card or the Business Platinum Rewards Card.",
  "note": "If you'd like me to proceed with enabling overdraft protection and/or applying for the Platinum card, reply YES and specify card type (personal Platinum Rewards or Business Platinum Rewards)."
}

{
  "message": "You’re all set — I’ve transferred you to a specialist with a summary of everything (overdraft enablement request, Platinum Rewards Card application, email-change notification confirmation, and debit-card scheduling). A human agent will pick up shortly and complete the remaining steps.",
  "what_happened": [
    "Transfer initiated to human agents (reason: specialized_department_required).",
    "Transfer summary sent: account actions performed, overdraft enable request + acceptance of $12.50 fee, request to apply for personal Platinum Rewards Card, and request to confirm any email-change notifications."
  ],
  "next": "A human agent will contact you to finish enabling overdraft protection, submit the credit card application, confirm emails sent, and schedule the Blue debit card standard delivery once eligible."
}
